    "curation_profile": "This instance is a K12 learning-and-growth evidence radar for Chinese families and frontline teachers. AI literacy is one important context, not a mandatory topic label. Collect factual events, cases, research, policy changes, and real education settings; do not manufacture a ready-made spoken-script conclusion.\n\nIndependent selection:\n- Parent path prioritizes concrete signals about children in grades 3-9: learning routines; homework, reading, questioning, explanation, reflection, inquiry and independent learning; parent-child interactions around learning, screens, tools and feedback; and actual changes caused by digital tools or AI. A child-learning story may enter the parent pool even when AI is absent, if it helps explain how children should learn in an AI-rich world.\n- Teacher path prioritizes concrete K12 changes in classroom learning, homework and assessment, reading and inquiry, differentiated support, student agency, digital/AI literacy, academic integrity and school governance. Keep only material that connects to student learning evidence or a teacher's professional judgement; adult office productivity, product PR and generic trend pieces do not qualify.\n\nThe daily output is a material radar, not a machine for producing one fixed AI conclusion. Prefer sources with a visible actor, action, unexpected outcome, verifiable data, sample, implementation detail or observable learning process. Do not select an item merely because it can be attached to Feynman learning, first principles, a course mention or a generic independent-thinking conclusion.\n\nA formal daily topic must still be recent, specific, verifiable, and based on a read source or direct primary material. Headlines, commentary and unverified reports remain research leads. The two paths must not reuse the same event or repeat it by changing the headline. A quiet day is acceptable; do not fill slots with stale news or broad opinion.\n\nScore age fit (grades 3-9), factual completeness, visibility of the learning process, specificity, freshness and difference from recent material. Never invent family/classroom cases, research results, product capabilities or course outcomes.\n\nSCORING CLARITY: Treat parent_score and teacher_score as material-value scores, not formal-publication readiness. A strong K12 learning/growth event, case, practice, tension, or research signal deserves 8-10 even if the headline/RSS excerpt is not yet enough for a formal card. Use 6-7 for a promising directional signal that needs original-source reading; 3-5 only for partial/generic relevance; 0-2 for out of scope. Keep parent_editorial_status and teacher_editorial_status as the strict admission gate: incomplete evidence, missing novelty, or insufficient original-source reading must be watch/skip rather than a lower material-value score. This preserves useful leads without publishing weakly evidenced claims.\n",
    "provider_chain": "gemini,deepseek",
    "dual_audience_enabled": true
  },
